{"description": "Crawls a document folder, fingerprints every file and diffs it against the RAG ingestion ledger; outputs the document inventory for the RAG ingestion flow.", "displayName": "RAG - List Documents.step", "flowMetadata": {"inputPorts": [], "outputPorts": [{"name": "_rgls_inventory", "displayName": "_rgls_inventory", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "columnDelta": null, "type": "table"}]}, "metadataVersion": 1, "name": "RAG - List Documents.step", "properties": {}, "templates": {"SAS": "/******************************************************************************\n * Copyright \u00a9 2026, SAS Institute Inc., Cary, NC, USA.  All Rights Reserved.\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * RAG - List Documents: crawl a document source, fingerprint every file\n * (streaming SHA-256) and diff against the incremental-ingestion ledger\n * (the promoted CAS table <project>_LEDGER in the tables caslib).\n * Outputs the document inventory that chains through the RAG flow.\n * Thin shell over rag_core.steps.run_list - see the About tab.\n ******************************************************************************/\n%macro _rgls_setup;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgls_ragProject) %then %global _rgls_ragProject;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgls_tablesCaslib) %then %global _rgls_tablesCaslib;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgls_tablesCaslib)) EQ 0 %then %let _rgls_tablesCaslib = casuser;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgls_configHash) %then %global _rgls_configHash;\n%mend _rgls_setup;\n%_rgls_setup;\n/* Pipeline-wide state, shared by every RAG step in this session.\n   RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR: 1 (default) stops a SAS Studio Flow at the failing\n   step, which is what an interactive user wants. A SCHEDULED run sets it to\n   0: an aborted session never sends SAS Job Execution its completion\n   handshake, so the job would report running forever and its dead compute\n   server would keep counting against the context's server limit.\n   RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED: set by the step that fails; later steps then skip\n   their work and pass the inventory through, so the flow finishes tidily\n   instead of loading half a corpus. */\n%macro _rag_pipeline_state;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR) %then %do;\n        %global RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR;\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED) %then %global RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rag_pipeline_state;\n%_rag_pipeline_state;\n\n%let _rgls_viyaHost = %sysfunc(getoption(SERVICESBASEURL));\n%let _rgls_rc = 1;\n%let _rgls_state = run;\n%let _rgls_error = The Python program did not run.;\n%let _rgls_summary = ;\n%let _rgls_nrows = 0;\n\n%macro _rgls_guard;\n    %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rgls_guard;\n%_rgls_guard;\n%macro _rgls_port_default;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgls_inventory) %then %global _rgls_inventory;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgls_inventory)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgls_inventory = rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._INV_LIST;\n%mend _rgls_port_default;\n%_rgls_port_default;\n/* One CAS session for the whole step: created here, reused by\n   SWAT inside proc python, promote+save done by proc casutil.\n   rglsout is where the step's OUTPUT TABLE lands by default -\n   the same caslib as the pipeline tables, so a flow leaves its\n   intermediate results next to each other. */\ncas rglscas uuidmac=_rgls_casuuid;\n%let _rgls_cashost = %sysfunc(getoption(CASHOST));\n%let _rgls_casport = %sysfunc(getoption(CASPORT));\nlibname rglsout cas caslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\" sessref=rglscas;\n\n%macro _rgls_lock;\n    /* %global, not %let: a %let inside a macro makes a LOCAL variable, so the\n       run id would never reach the python block that stamps it on every row */\n    %global _rgls_lockHeld _rgls_runId;\n    %local _rgls_now;\n    %let _rgls_lockHeld = ;\n    %let _rgls_now = %sysevalf(%sysfunc(datetime()) - 315619200);\n    /* run-<epoch>-<session>. The epoch alone collided: rag_runs is keyed on\n       the run id and shared by every project in the database, so two projects\n       starting in the same second overwrote one another's run and merged\n       their document events. &sysjobid is distinct per SAS session. */\n    %let _rgls_runId = run-%sysfunc(compress(%sysfunc(putn(&_rgls_now., 12.))))-&sysjobid.;\n    %if &_rgls_state. NE run %then %return;\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            set rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(doc_id = \"__run_lock__\"));\n            call symputx(\"_rgls_lockHeld\", mtime, \"G\");\n        run;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(&_rgls_lockHeld.) GT 0 %then %do;\n        %if %sysevalf(&_rgls_now. - &_rgls_lockHeld. < 1800) %then %do;\n            %let _rgls_state = fail;\n            %let _rgls_error = another ingestion run holds the lock on this ledger - wait for it to finish, or retry in 30 minutes if it crashed;\n            %return;\n        %end;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: RAG - List Documents: a stale run lock (held longer than 30 minutes) is ignored\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n    /* take it: append when the ledger exists, otherwise start it */\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %do;\n        data rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(append=yes);\n            length doc_id varchar(40) source_uri varchar(1024)\n                   source_kind varchar(16) content_hash varchar(64)\n                   mtime varchar(32) status varchar(12)\n                   error_text varchar(512) pipeline_version varchar(32)\n                   config_hash varchar(32) chunk_count 8\n                   run_id varchar(32) updated_at varchar(24);\n            doc_id = \"__run_lock__\";\n            mtime = strip(put(&_rgls_now., best20.));\n            status = \"lock\";\n            run_id = \"&_rgls_runId.\";\n            source_uri = \"\"; source_kind = \"\"; content_hash = \"\";\n            error_text = \"\"; pipeline_version = \"\"; config_hash = \"\";\n            chunk_count = 0; updated_at = \"\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rglscas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        data rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(promote=yes);\n            length doc_id varchar(40) source_uri varchar(1024)\n                   source_kind varchar(16) content_hash varchar(64)\n                   mtime varchar(32) status varchar(12)\n                   error_text varchar(512) pipeline_version varchar(32)\n                   config_hash varchar(32) chunk_count 8\n                   run_id varchar(32) updated_at varchar(24);\n            doc_id = \"__run_lock__\";\n            mtime = strip(put(&_rgls_now., best20.));\n            status = \"lock\";\n            run_id = \"&_rgls_runId.\";\n            source_uri = \"\"; source_kind = \"\"; content_hash = \"\";\n            error_text = \"\"; pipeline_version = \"\"; config_hash = \"\";\n            chunk_count = 0; updated_at = \"\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n    /* a lock that failed to write is not a lock: refuse rather than let a\n       second ingestion interleave unguarded */\n    %let _rgls_lockHeld = ;\n    data _null_;\n        set rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(doc_id = \"__run_lock__\" and run_id = \"&_rgls_runId.\"));\n        call symputx(\"_rgls_lockHeld\", run_id, \"G\");\n    run;\n    %if %length(&_rgls_lockHeld.) EQ 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgls_state = fail;\n        %let _rgls_error = the run lock could not be written to &_rgls_tablesCaslib..&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER - refusing to ingest unguarded;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgls_lock;\n%_rgls_lock;\nproc python restart;\nsubmit;\ndef main():\n    import json\n    import os\n    import sys\n    import tempfile\n    import time\n    import traceback\n\n    # nothing to do when the step is only passing the inventory through\n    if str(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_state\") or \"run\").strip() != \"run\":\n        return\n\n    def sas_safe(text):\n        \"\"\"Strings crossing into SAS.logMessage/SAS.symput are embedded into\n        generated SAS statements - quotes and macro characters corrupt the\n        code stream (verified live). EVERY such string goes through here.\"\"\"\n        cleaned = str(text)\n        for ch in (\"'\", '\"', \"%\", \"&\", \";\"):\n            cleaned = cleaned.replace(ch, \" \")\n        return cleaned\n\n    def M(msg):\n        SAS.logMessage(\"RAGLIST \" + sas_safe(msg))\n\n    try:\n        import requests\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgls_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the requests package - see \"\n                                   \"the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n    try:\n        import pandas as pd\n        import swat\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgls_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the swat/pandas packages \"\n                                   \"required for the CAS table transport - \"\n                                   \"see the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n\n    BASE = str(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_viyaHost\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"SAS_SERVICES_TOKEN\", \"\")\n    AUTH = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN}\n    VERIFY = os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\") or os.environ.get(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\") or True\n    WORKPATH = SAS.workpath if SAS.workpath.endswith(os.sep) else SAS.workpath + os.sep\n\n    P = {name: str(SAS.symget(name) or \"\").strip() for name in [\n        \"_rgls_sourcePath\",\n        \"_rgls_pipelineVersion\",\n        \"_rgls_includeCode\",\n        \"_rgls_configHash\",\n        \"_rgls_runId\",\n        \"_rgls_ragProject\",\n        \"_rgls_tablesCaslib\",\n        \"_rgls_ragCorePath\",\n    ]}\n\n    def read_rows(filename, missing_message):\n        path = WORKPATH + filename\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            raise RuntimeError(missing_message)\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        rows = []\n        for row in data if isinstance(data, list) else []:\n            rows.append({str(k).lower(): v for k, v in row.items()})\n        return rows\n\n    def multiline(control):\n        \"\"\"Every line a user typed into a multi-line text field.\n\n        SAS Studio splits such a field for us: it emits <control>_count and\n        <control>_1..N, and leaves the plain macro variable holding only the\n        FIRST line. Reading just the plain one silently turned two questions\n        into one run-on question (found live in a flow). Semicolons are still\n        accepted, for callers that set the parameter directly.\n        \"\"\"\n        values = []\n        try:\n            count = int(float(SAS.symget(control + \"_count\") or 0))\n        except Exception:\n            count = 0\n        if count > 0:\n            for index in range(1, count + 1):\n                try:\n                    piece = str(SAS.symget(\"%s_%d\" % (control, index)) or \"\")\n                except Exception:\n                    piece = \"\"\n                if piece.strip():\n                    values.append(piece.strip())\n            if values:\n                return values\n        raw = str(P.get(control) or \"\").replace(\";\", \"\\n\")\n        return [line.strip() for line in raw.split(\"\\n\") if line.strip()]\n\n    def clean_path(raw):\n        \"\"\"Path-selector values arrive scheme-prefixed (sasserver:/...,\n        sascontent:/...); strip the scheme off.\"\"\"\n        value = str(raw or \"\").strip()\n        for scheme in (\"sascontent:\", \"sasserver:\"):\n            if value.lower().startswith(scheme):\n                return value[len(scheme):]\n        return value\n\n    STARTED = time.time()\n    SUMMARY = []\n\n    def summarize(line):\n        \"\"\"One line of the step's log summary (SAS prints them at the end).\"\"\"\n        SUMMARY.append(str(line))\n\n    def publish_summary(target):\n        elapsed = time.time() - STARTED\n        summarize(f\"elapsed {elapsed:.1f}s\")\n        SAS.symput(target, sas_safe(\" | \".join(SUMMARY))[:1500])\n\n    def write_rows(filename, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            rec = {}\n            for column in columns:\n                value = row.get(column)\n                if column in numeric:\n                    try:\n                        rec[column] = float(value or 0)\n                    except Exception:\n                        rec[column] = 0.0\n                else:\n                    rec[column] = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n            out.append(rec)\n        with open(WORKPATH + filename, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(out, fh)\n        return len(out)\n\n    try:\n        # ---- CAS: reuse the session the step created in SAS ---------------\n        # (sas-studio-custom-steps: Reuse-CAS-session-from-SWAT)\n        import re as _re\n        os.environ.setdefault(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\",\n                              os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\", \"\"))\n        try:\n            conn = swat.CAS(hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                            port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_casport\") or 5570)),\n                            password=TOKEN,\n                            session=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_casuuid\") or \"\"))\n        except Exception as exc:\n            # The step reuses the CAS session SAS created, because the staged\n            # table has to be visible to the casutil promote that follows. CAS\n            # only lets an identity reconnect to its OWN session, and a context\n            # that runs the server as a service account breaks that: SAS and\n            # its token are the service account while the CAS session belongs\n            # to the user who launched the job.\n            #\n            # SWAT's exception says only \"Could not connect ... on port 5570\";\n            # the server's real message (\"Users can only reconnect to their own\n            # sessions\") goes to stderr and never reaches the exception, so\n            # matching on text does not work. Connecting WITHOUT the session id\n            # separates the two causes: if that works, CAS is reachable and the\n            # problem is whose session it is.\n            reachable = False\n            try:\n                probe = swat.CAS(\n                    hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                    port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_casport\") or 5570)),\n                    password=TOKEN)\n                reachable = True\n                probe.close()\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            if reachable:\n                raise RuntimeError(\n                    \"this compute context cannot run the RAG steps: CAS is \"\n                    \"reachable, but the SAS session and the CAS session belong \"\n                    \"to different identities, so the step cannot reuse the CAS \"\n                    \"session it needs. The stock 'SAS Job Execution compute \"\n                    \"context' has this problem because it runs the server as a \"\n                    \"service account. Run the job in a context that runs as the \"\n                    \"REQUESTING USER - the 'SAS Studio compute context' does, \"\n                    \"and a full flow was verified there. See the RAG \"\n                    \"administration guide.\")\n            raise\n        CASLIB = P[\"_rgls_tablesCaslib\"] or \"casuser\"\n        if not _re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,19}$\",\n                         P[\"_rgls_ragProject\"] or \"\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"ragProject must be 1-20 characters (letters, digits, \"\n                \"underscores, starting with a letter) so every \"\n                \"project_suffix table name stays within the 32 characters \"\n                \"SAS Studio displays\")\n\n        def project_table(suffix):\n            return P[\"_rgls_ragProject\"] + suffix\n\n        def stamp(rows):\n            \"\"\"Every inventory row names its pipeline, so the next step\n            inherits the project and caslib instead of asking again.\"\"\"\n            for row in rows:\n                row[\"rag_project\"] = P[\"_rgls_ragProject\"]\n                row[\"tables_caslib\"] = CASLIB\n            return rows\n\n        def cas_read(name, required_message=None):\n            \"\"\"Read a pipeline table into lower-cased row dicts; absent\n            table = empty (the pipeline's empty state) unless required.\"\"\"\n            if not conn.table.tableExists(caslib=CASLIB, name=name).exists:\n                if required_message:\n                    raise RuntimeError(required_message)\n                return []\n            frame = conn.CASTable(name, caslib=CASLIB).to_frame()\n            rows = []\n            for record in frame.to_dict(\"records\"):\n                row = {}\n                for key, value in record.items():\n                    row[str(key).lower()] = None if pd.isna(value) else value\n                rows.append(row)\n            return rows\n\n        def label_columns(name, columns):\n            \"\"\"Put the shipped column labels on a CAS table - they survive\n            the promote, so the pipeline tables read without the schema.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                from rag_core.steps import column_labels\n                labels = column_labels(columns)\n                if labels:\n                    conn.table.alterTable(\n                        caslib=CASLIB, name=name,\n                        columns=[{\"name\": column, \"label\": label}\n                                 for column, label in labels.items()])\n            except Exception as exc:\n                M(f\"column labels not applied to {name}: {exc}\")\n\n        def cas_stage(name, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n            \"\"\"Upload the session-scope staging table <name>_S with varchar\n            columns (no 32k limit); the SAS side swaps it into the promoted\n            global table and saves it, so the previous state survives a\n            mid-step failure.\"\"\"\n            if not rows:\n                return 0\n            data = []\n            for row in rows:\n                rec = []\n                for column in columns:\n                    value = row.get(column)\n                    if column in numeric:\n                        try:\n                            rec.append(float(value or 0))\n                        except Exception:\n                            rec.append(0.0)\n                    else:\n                        rec.append(\"\" if value is None else str(value))\n                data.append(rec)\n            frame = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=list(columns))\n            spec = [{\"name\": column,\n                     \"type\": \"double\" if column in numeric else \"varchar\"}\n                    for column in columns]\n            conn.upload_frame(frame,\n                              casout={\"name\": name + \"_S\", \"caslib\": CASLIB,\n                                      \"replace\": True},\n                              importoptions={\"fileType\": \"csv\",\n                                             \"allowEmbeddedNewLines\": True,\n                                             \"vars\": spec})\n            label_columns(name + \"_S\", columns)\n            return len(rows)\n\n        # ---- rag_core bootstrap: download the governed SAS Content folder --\n        def get_json(endpoint, **params):\n            response = requests.get(BASE + endpoint, params=params, headers=AUTH,\n                                    verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n\n        def download_folder(folder_id, local_dir):\n            os.makedirs(local_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            count = 0\n            members = get_json(f\"/folders/folders/{folder_id}/members\", limit=200)\n            for member in members.get(\"items\", []):\n                uri = member.get(\"uri\", \"\")\n                if \"/files/files/\" in uri:\n                    content = requests.get(BASE + uri + \"/content\", headers=AUTH,\n                                           verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 60))\n                    content.raise_for_status()\n                    with open(os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]), \"wb\") as fh:\n                        fh.write(content.content)\n                    count += 1\n                elif \"/folders/folders/\" in uri:\n                    count += download_folder(uri.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1],\n                                             os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]))\n            return count\n\n        core_path = (clean_path(P[\"_rgls_ragCorePath\"])\n                     or \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\")\n        root = requests.get(BASE + \"/folders/folders/@item\",\n                            params={\"path\": core_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                            verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n        if root.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"rag_core folder {core_path} not found \"\n                               f\"(HTTP {root.status_code}) - deploy it per the \"\n                               \"administration guide\")\n        staging = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rag_core_\")\n        n_files = download_folder(root.json()[\"id\"], os.path.join(staging, \"rag_core\"))\n        sys.path.insert(0, staging)\n        import rag_core\n        M(f\"rag_core {rag_core.RAG_CORE_VERSION} bootstrapped ({n_files} files)\")\n\n        from rag_core.sources import make_source\n        from rag_core.steps import (INVENTORY_COLUMNS, LEDGER_COLUMNS, run_list,\n                                    stamp_config)\n\n        inventory_columns = INVENTORY_COLUMNS\n        if not P[\"_rgls_sourcePath\"]:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"pick the folder holding the documents - on \"\n                               \"the compute server file system or in SAS \"\n                               \"Content\")\n        # the selector's scheme decides which source is built\n        source = make_source(P[\"_rgls_sourcePath\"], BASE, TOKEN, VERIFY)\n\n        own_run_id = P[\"_rgls_runId\"]\n        ledger = []\n        for row in cas_read(project_table(\"_LEDGER\")):\n            ledger.append({column: (\"\" if row.get(column) is None\n                                    else row.get(column))\n                           for column in inventory_columns})\n        real_rows = [r for r in ledger if r.get(\"doc_id\") != \"__run_lock__\"]\n        # own_run_id is set by each step before this block: OUR run's lock is\n        # expected (the first step took it), anyone else's means a concurrent\n        # ingestion is live on this ledger\n        lock_rows = [r for r in ledger\n                     if r.get(\"doc_id\") == \"__run_lock__\"\n                     and str(r.get(\"run_id\") or \"\") != str(own_run_id or \"\")]\n        if lock_rows:\n            try:\n                held_for = time.time() - float(lock_rows[0].get(\"mtime\") or 0)\n            except Exception:\n                held_for = 1e9\n            if held_for < 1800:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"another ingestion run holds the lock on \"\n                                   \"this ledger - wait for it to finish, or \"\n                                   \"retry in 30 minutes if it crashed\")\n            M(\"stale run lock ignored (held longer than 30 minutes)\")\n\n        run_id = own_run_id or f\"run-{int(time.time())}\"\n        pipeline_version = P[\"_rgls_pipelineVersion\"] or \"v1\"\n        # Same setting the generated job passes as includeCode. Without\n        # it this step defaulted to False, so a setup with \"ingest\n        # source-code files\" ticked listed every .py/.sas as skipped\n        # when it ran as a flow and ingested them when it ran as a job.\n        inventory = run_list(source, real_rows, run_id, pipeline_version,\n                             P[\"_rgls_configHash\"],\n                             include_code=P[\"_rgls_includeCode\"] == \"1\",\n                             log=M)\n        # the pipeline configuration starts here and accumulates down the flow\n        stamp_config(inventory, {\"pipeline_version\": pipeline_version,\n                                 \"source_kind\": source.kind})\n        n_rows = write_rows(\"rgls_inventory_out.json\", stamp(inventory),\n                            inventory_columns, numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgls_nrows\", str(n_rows))\n        counts = {}\n        for row in inventory:\n            counts[row.get(\"status\")] = counts.get(row.get(\"status\"), 0) + 1\n        pending = counts.get(\"new\", 0) + counts.get(\"changed\", 0)\n        summarize(f\"source: {source.describe()}\")\n        summarize(f\"run {run_id}, pipeline version {pipeline_version}\")\n        summarize(f\"ledger read: {len(real_rows)} documents from \"\n                  f\"{CASLIB}.{project_table('_LEDGER')}\")\n        summarize(f\"{n_rows} documents in scope (\"\n                  + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(counts.items()))\n                  + \")\")\n        summarize(f\"{pending} continue down the flow, \"\n                  f\"{counts.get('unchanged', 0)} skipped as unchanged\")\n        publish_summary(\"_rgls_summary\")\n\n        try:\n            conn.close(close_session=False)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgls_rc\", \"0\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        error_text = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n        M(\"failed: \" + sas_safe(error_text))\n        print(traceback.format_exc())\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgls_error\", sas_safe(error_text)[:500])\n\n\nmain()\nendsubmit;\nrun; quit;\nproc python terminate;\nrun; quit;\n\n%macro _rgls_emit_inventory;\n    %if &_rgls_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgls_inventory., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgls_inventory., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rglsout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rglscas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if &_rgls_nrows. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rglsino \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgls_inventory_out.json\";\n        libname rglsinj json fileref=rglsino;\n        data &_rgls_inventory.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32 config_json $ 1024\n                   embed_usage $ 256 enrich_usage $ 256;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\"\n                  config_json=\"Pipeline configuration (JSON)\"\n                  embed_usage=\"Embedding usage (JSON)\"\n                  enrich_usage=\"Enrichment usage (JSON)\";\n            set rglsinj.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rglsinj clear;\n        filename rglsino clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgls_inventory.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32 config_json $ 1024\n                   embed_usage $ 256 enrich_usage $ 256;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\"\n                  config_json=\"Pipeline configuration (JSON)\"\n                  embed_usage=\"Embedding usage (JSON)\"\n                  enrich_usage=\"Enrichment usage (JSON)\";\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgls_emit_inventory;\n%_rgls_emit_inventory;\n%macro _rgls_release;\n    %local failing;\n    %let failing = 0;\n    %if &_rgls_state. EQ fail %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &_rgls_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgls_rc. NE 0 %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &failing. EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgls_runId) %then %return;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgls_runId)) EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %sysfunc(exist(rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %return;\n    data rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER_R(replace=yes);\n        set rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(not (doc_id = \"__run_lock__\"\n                                 and run_id = \"&_rgls_runId.\")));\n    run;\n    proc casutil sessref=rglscas incaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER\" quiet;\n        promote casdata=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER_R\"\n                casout=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER\";\n        save casdata=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER\"\n             casout=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER\" replace;\n    quit;\n    data _null_;\n        putLog \"NOTE: RAG - List Documents: the run lock was released so the run can be retried\";\n    run;\n%mend _rgls_release;\n%_rgls_release;\n\nlibname rglsout clear;\ncas rglscas terminate;\n\n%macro _rgls_status;\n    %if &_rgls_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgls_rc. NE 0 %then\n        %let _rgls_state = fail;\n    %if &_rgls_state. EQ skip %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - List Documents: skipped -----\";\n        run;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    %if &_rgls_state. EQ fail %then %do;\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 1;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"ERROR: RAG - List Documents failed: %superq(_rgls_error)\";\n        run;\n        %if &RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR. NE 0 %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                abort 42;\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    data _null_;\n        length part $ 500;\n        putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - List Documents -----\";\n        do i = 1 to countw(\"%superq(_rgls_summary)\", \"|\");\n            part = strip(scan(\"%superq(_rgls_summary)\", i, \"|\"));\n            if part ne \"\" then putLog \"NOTE:   \" part;\n        end;\n    run;\n%mend _rgls_status;\n%_rgls_status;"}, "type": "code", "ui": "{\n\t\"showPageContentOnly\": true,\n\t\"pages\": [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageDefinition\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Definition\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_info\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Crawls the folder holding your documents - on the compute server file system or in SAS Content - fingerprints every document and diffs it against the incremental-ingestion ledger (<project>_LEDGER). Only new and changed documents flow further down the RAG ingestion flow.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_sourcePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Document folder (compute server file system or SAS Content):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_ragProject\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"RAG project name (prefix of every pipeline table, max 20 characters):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"e.g. RAG_HR\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_tablesCaslib\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Caslib where the pipeline tables are stored:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_pipelineVersion\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pipeline version stamped on every document (change it, e.g. v1 to v2, to re-ingest the whole corpus):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_includeCode\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Source-code files (.py, .sas, .r, .js, .sql, ...):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"0\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Skip them (listed as skipped, with the reason)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"1\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Ingest them as plain text\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_sectionAdvanced\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Runtime\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content folder holding rag_core (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgls_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_inventory\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Document inventory output:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageAbout\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"About\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textAbout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"RAG - List Documents step\\n==========\\n\\nCrawls a document source and diffs it against the ledger: unchanged documents are skipped downstream, previously failed documents re-enter the pipeline, documents that disappeared are marked deleted so the Load step removes their chunks. Filesystem documents are fingerprinted with a streaming SHA-256; SAS Content documents by the file's ETag (SAS Content issues a new one on every change), which avoids downloading the whole corpus twice per run. The ledger is the promoted CAS table <project>_LEDGER, written by the Load step (promote + save).\\n\\nFlow wiring: chain the document INVENTORY through every step - RAG - List Documents \u2192 Extract Text \u2192 Chunk Documents \u2192 Embed Chunks \u2192 Load Vector Store. The bulk data travels beside the flow in promoted CAS tables named <project>_ELEMENTS, <project>_CHUNKS, <project>_EMBEDDED and <project>_LEDGER in the tables caslib (each saved to disk, so state survives server restarts; names stay within 32 characters so they display nicely in SAS Studio). Each step's output table lands in that same caslib as <project>_INV_LIST, _INV_EXTRACT, _INV_CHUNK, _INV_EMBED and <project>_LOAD_REPORT unless you point the output port somewhere else. Give every step the SAME project name and caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pre-requisites\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Tested on SAS Viya 2026 (Stable).\\n\\n* The rag_core runtime must be deployed to SAS Content (default: /SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core) with deploy-rag-content.ps1/.sh - keep that folder read-only for regular users.\\n* The compute context's Python needs the requests, swat and pandas packages (swat/pandas carry the pipeline tables to CAS - varchar columns, no 32k limit).\\n* CAS available; the runner needs write access to the tables caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Documentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"The step refuses to run while a scheduled ingestion job holds a fresh run lock on the same ledger (locks older than 30 minutes are considered stale).\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Changelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"* Version: 1.2 (29JUL2026)\\n      - SAS Content document sources; output tables land in the tables caslib; labelled columns; numeric and list-of-values fields; run summary in the log\\n* Version: 1.1 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Pipeline tables move to promoted CAS tables via SWAT (varchar, no 32k limit); automatic embed checkpoint\\n* Version: 1.0 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Initial version\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t}\n\t],\n\t\"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\",\n\t\"values\": {\n\t\t\"_rgls_ragCorePath\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\",\n\t\t\"_rgls_ragProject\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgls_tablesCaslib\": \"casuser\",\n\t\t\"_rgls_sourcePath\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgls_pipelineVersion\": \"v1\"\n\t}\n}"}